AtrisShare does not bundle AtrisAgent source, AI CLI executables, FFmpeg,
FFprobe, whisper.cpp executables or speech models. Those remain external tools
and assets with their own licenses and terms.

Native staging includes pinned Node.js, bundled local API and official-SDK MCP
server, and the application LICENSE and NOTICE. Generated runtime resources
contain the Node license inventory and full license/notice texts collected for
the API/MCP bundles, installed frontend dependency closure and locked,
target-filtered Cargo dependency graph (including build dependencies).
dependency-inventory.json records coverage, text hashes, source provenance and
limitations; manifest.json records the exact staged resource hashes. These are
inventory checks, not a declaration that all distribution obligations are met.

Unmodified Cargo source archives are linked in RUST-THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt,
including source for MPL-covered components. Preserve their notices and source
availability when redistributing. System libraries, WebView2, installer tooling
and external tools/models require their own distribution review. See
docs/PACKAGING.md for the unsigned/manual-update preview policy and final gate.
